# Docker build-context exclusions.
#
# infra/Dockerfile.api (and, from M3, infra/Dockerfile.web) build with the REPO ROOT as
# context (`build: {context: .., dockerfile: infra/Dockerfile.*}` in infra/docker-compose.yml).
# Without this file every `docker build` would tar up node_modules, .venv, caches and any
# local data before the daemon starts resolving layers. Most entries here change build-context
# size only, never image contents — the one deliberate exception is worker/prompts/*.md, negated
# below: `COPY worker ./worker` needs the shipped prompt files at runtime (`load_prompt`).

# VCS / editor / local tool state
.git/
.claude/
.superpowers/

# node / pnpm
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
.next/
**/.next/

# python
.venv/
**/.venv/
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
**/.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
.import_linter_cache/
**/.import_linter_cache/

# coverage / build artifacts
coverage/
**/coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo

# secrets — **/-anchored so nested env files (web/.env.local, ...) are excluded too, not just
# the context root. The negation is deliberately root-anchored: only the tracked
# .env.example is re-allowed.
**/.env*
!.env.example

# data that must never enter an image
honeypot/data/
*.mmdb
evals/results/

# docs — not needed inside any image
docs/
*.md
!worker/prompts/*.md
